ADDITIONAL TERMS – WATERMARK AND ANTI-PLAGIARISM PROTECTION (Pineapple Games)

1. Watermark Protection:
   This codebase includes visible and invisible watermarks to prevent plagiarism
   and unauthorized copying:
   - Visual watermark (CSS class .pg-watermark) displayed only inside game pages
     (/games/*) with contact info: pineapplevacorp@gmail.com and official X/Twitter
     https://x.com/pineapplevacorp
   - Console watermark and security warnings printed on every page load via
     assets/js/site.js, including build info, origin, and legal references
   - Automatic restoration: if the watermark DOM node is removed, a
     MutationObserver re-injects it (games only)

2. No Removal:
   You may not remove, obscure, or alter any watermark, console notice, or
   attribution (including the corner/diagonal Pineapple Games marks) from the
   games. The watermark is part of the integrity protection of the Software.

3. Anti-Plagiarism:
   Copying the code, assets, or game logic without permission violates:
   - Terms and Conditions: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/terminos/
   - DMCA / Copyright Policy: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/dmca/
   - Privacy Policy: https://pineappleva.github.io/Games/legal/privacidad/
   - This LICENSE file (MIT + this additional clause)
   If you want to reuse any part of our work for a project, video, or similar,
   contact us first at pineapplevacorp@gmail.com — we usually say yes when asked
   politely.

4. Security Notice:
   The console prints a Self-XSS warning. Do not paste code you do not understand.
   For vulnerability reports, contact pineapplevacorp@gmail.com.
   Official X/Twitter: https://x.com/pineapplevacorp

5. License Detection:
   This file is intentionally structured to remain detectable by GitHub as MIT
   License (standard MIT text at top), with these additional anti-plagiarism
   terms appended. The MIT permissions still apply, subject to the watermark
   preservation requirement above.
